   "description": "Longing is the acute, aching desire for something not yet possessed or not yet reached — a desire too strong to be satisfied by substitutes. The Hebrew and Greek vocabulary here covers yearning and eager, almost straining expectation. Longing appears in the psalms as the deep thirst for God himself (as the deer pants for water); it appears in Paul as the groaning of creation and the eager expectation of glory. Longing is the inner posture of the person who knows what they were made for and has not yet arrived there.",
